{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"✨Fuddles✨","id":"403783497564684291","is_bot":0,"username":"fuddlescottage"},"author_id":"403783497564684291","channel_id":"851195612049309766","content":"(Please dont. Lets talk dm me please. We want you to have fun for the whole season.)","created_at":"2021-08-23T04:29:07.334000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"879220688773316628","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"StarPilot94","id":"468162764586876949","is_bot":0,"username":"starpilot94"},"author_id":"468162764586876949","channel_id":"851195612049309766","content":"Secel gets up from her napping spot against an unused headstone. Stretching out, she groaned at the stiffness of her joints. Then, after standing up finally, she looked around. Knowing the truth somehow made everything more… wicked. It hurt more than she wanted to believe. \n\nBut despite this, she couldn’t say no to this. She owed it to herself, to the people she had fought to save, the people she had bled for. The ones who would never see the light of day again.\n\nGrabbing hold of a shovel, she began digging. The digging wasn’t the hard part, but the weight was unsettling. Eventually she set up the first line of new graves, and did her best to do the traditions of the countless other religions followed by the thousands upon thousands of deceased. But those who she didn’t know anything about got the burial she had grown up with. \n\nWhen it came to the dead British, she allocated a section to them. When it came to the dead soldiers that had saved the city by turning it to ruin, they got their own section. The dead civilians took up the majority.\n\nBy the time she finally stopped, she couldn’t help but feel like her task was far, far from over. She then turned to getting the plans for her new home designed. In keeping with tradition, the building would be in the style of the Ancient Greek buildings, with enough space for possibly a small family to live in. Looking down into the hole that was the basement, she sighs and pulls the Demon Armor out of the hole. \n\n“I think this should work?” She asks out loud before tracing the space with her finger. “Should being the key word. Don’t get your hopes up Secel. Just because you’re doing this doesn’t mean he’ll want you if you tell him.”","created_at":"2021-08-23T18:06:02.492000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"879426273246576701","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"StarPilot94","id":"468162764586876949","is_bot":0,"username":"starpilot94"},"author_id":"468162764586876949","channel_id":"851195612049309766","content":"Secel sighs as she finishes three more groups of graves. She wasn’t tired, but more lonely. She switched to the dress she bought for weddings just for a change of clothes and pinned it so it only comes down to her shins before making her way to the Noir","created_at":"2021-08-24T00:49:27.255000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"879527795380875264","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
